\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
For a number field $K$, does an algorithm exist that takes an arbitrary multivariable polynomial with coefficients in $K$ and decides whether it has a zero in $K$? Determine for which number fields such a decision procedure exists. Solutions are sought in the field $K$ itself.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a number field $K$, does an algorithm exist that takes an arbitrary multivariable polynomial with coefficients in $K$ and decides whether it has a zero in $K$? Determine for which number fields such a decision procedure exists. Solutions are sought in the field $K$ itself.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 1222 (NT-031). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://math.mit.edu/~poonen/papers/htp.pdf}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:1222}

